    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5516A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to the central pine barrens area and the core preservation\narea\n\nPURPOSE:  To correct the description of acreage added to the central\npine barrens area and the core preservation area by Chapter 240 of the\nLaws of 2013.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:  Chapter 240 of the Laws of 2013 added the area\nknown as the Carmans River Watershed to the Pine Barrens Preserve\nlocated in eastern Long Island. The area added consisted of\napproximately 3875 total acres with 1660 acres thereof in the core\narea. Those areas were particularly described in that Chapter. This\nbill amends subdivision 10 and 11 of section 510107 of the\nenvironmental conservation law to make corrections and clarifications\nto those descriptions.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  The bill is correcting the description in the prior\nlegislation.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: Immediately.\n\n",
